Sets, relations, propositional logic, predicate logic, mathematical reasoning, proof
techniques. Sequences and summation, mathematical induction. Counting, permutation,
combination, and discrete probability. Number theory. Logic programming, graphs, trees,
and related algorithms. Finite automata, context-free grammar, and the Turing machine.
