This is a study of indigenous knowledge in different regions of Thailand with a
holistic approach, including analyses from scientific, technological, social science and
anthropological perspectives.

Students will learn how to appreciate the value of indigenous
knowledge and recognize the ways in which such knowledge has been accumulated—
lifelong learning of indigenous people and knowledge transfer between generations. Students will learn to become systematic, self-taught learners.

